pr.md · handed back 14:13 by andres · 5 notes · drafted by claude
STET  "Intro paragraph here" — do not change
DOC   #5 "too long overall"
#6    note  "second item" — say why
#7    no    ## Details (whole section)
#8    ask   "detail one" — is this right?   (answer only; don't edit)
next: 1) Edit pr.md with your Edit tool (not Write). Change only what the notes ask.
      2) Record what you did, one line per note, then run:
birta respond pr.md <<'EOF'
#6 done
#6 covers "<words you wrote>"
#7 done
#7 covers "<words you wrote>"
#8 answer: <your answer>
#5 done: <one line: what you changed for this whole-doc note>
#5 covers "<words you wrote>"
@: <one or two lines to the reviewer in first person ("I cut…"); no questions here>
EOF
      Per note you can write instead:  #N didnt: <why>   or   #N answer: <reply>
      To cite a note or an answer:     #N covers "<words you wrote>"   one per edit
      To ask the reviewer:             ask "<exact words in the doc>": <question>
      For a change no note asked for:  unasked "<exact words you added or removed>": <why>
      `no` means the reviewer wants that text gone; cut it, or say why not with didnt.
      3) Then wait again: birta review pr.md --wait
